  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In July 2026 remarks, Barr said AI could transform the economy and benefit lower- and middle-income workers, but also warned it could exacerbate inequality by eliminating some jobs while boosting higher-income individuals' income and wealth. He said the future is uncertain, making scenarios useful, and described a policy challenge of considering education, job training, competition, tax policy, and other areas so AI gains are shared broadly rather than accruing to a small group. In April 2025 remarks, Barr discussed responsible innovation in generative AI in banking, citing potential benefits alongside the need to manage risks, and later focused on risks including deepfakes and cybercrime.",
